    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nI updated local to be on revision 088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636 and I'm getting this error.  It seems like if there's no info available for the item, this pops up but I am not 100% sure of the cause.  Just going off of where the error is occurring.\n\nIt's not a noisy error for me, but this is with both mini.snippets and intelephense attached to a buffer.  This wasn't happening when I was on the commit that snippet's `lsp_server` feature was first introduced, so it seems very specific to a (recent) change to `mini.completion`.\n\nI *think* if you check whether the event has the col & width properties and if not exit out of the function by some means, that would solve this?  But maybe there's a better idea.  It just seems like when completion is trying to render the info/preview window it's not able to under certain scenarios.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.completion/blob/main/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1475\n\n```\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../site/pack/rocks/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1475: attempt to perform arithmetic on field 'col' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n\t.../site/pack/rocks/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1475: in function 'info_window_options'\n\t.../site/pack/rocks/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1383: in function ''\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```",
