        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> SInce I can't find a consistent means of reproducing, do you have any suggestions on capturing what caused the event to not have the `col` property? I don't mind editing local files for the purpose of trying to resolve this if nothing else, but I would like to capture the cause not just the effect.\n\nEvent is captured on every 'CompleteChanged' event ([here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L909)). Before [actually using](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1475-L1476) its `col` / `width` / `scrollbar` properties (which should always be present inside callback of 'CompleteChanged' event, `:h v:event`) there is a check that [event is still present](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1369). So that means that somehow event table is corrupted either before it is stored (likely some outside influence) or after (I don't see anything in 'mini.completion' that affects that).\n\nAre you sure you don't have something interfering with built-in completion? Like still enabled `vim.lsp.completion` or something else that might look like affecting relevant events?\n\nI'd try adding some logging, try to reproduce, and examine latest logged elements. Something like:\n- Add a `_G.log = {}` call somewhere inside 'lua/mini/completion'.lua.\n- Add `table.insert(_G.log, { state = 'auto_info', col = H.info.event.col, item = H.info.event.completed_item })` after [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L909).\n- Add `table.insert(_G.log, { state = 'show_info_window', col = H.info.event.col, item = H.info.event.completed_item })` after [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1369).\n- Try to reproduce and see last items of `:=log`.",
