        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Are you sure you don't have something interfering with built-in completion? Like still enabled vim.lsp.completion or something else that might look like affecting relevant events?\n\nI don't use `vim.lsp.completion` anymore since that conflicts with mini.completion.  I did also add this, and not sure if this may be causing issues?\n\n```lua\nlocal kind_priority = {\n    Text = -1, -- don't show buffer text as completion items\n    Snippet = 99,\n}\n\nlocal opts = {\n    filtersort = \"fuzzy\",\n    kind_priority = kind_priority,\n}\n\nlocal process_items = function(items, base)\n    return completion.default_process_items(items, base, opts)\nend\n\ncompletion.setup({\n    lsp_completion = {\n        source_func = \"omnifunc\",\n        process_items = process_items,\n    },\n})\n````\n\nI do have these though for `vim.opt`, but I don't think this would cause an issue:\n\n```lua\nlocal o = vim.o\n\no.completeopt = \"fuzzy,menuone,noinsert,popup,preview\"\n\no.shortmess:append(\"c\")\n```\n\nIn the mean time I'll add those logging lines and see if I can reproduce.",
