            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ```lua\n> local o = vim.o\n> \n> o.completeopt = \"fuzzy,menuone,noinsert,popup,preview\"\n> ```\n\nWhy do you have both 'popup' and 'preview' in 'completeopt' when they 1) conflict with each other; and 2) conflict with what info window does, as they both \"Show extra information about the currently selected completion ...\"?\n\nThe [suggested 'completeopt' value](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/90ab64f944a5a63a9efebe6735e1f2c6d4db3613/doc/mini-completion.txt#L86-L87) is `\"menuone,noselect,fuzzy\"`. Using 'noinsert' instead of 'noselect' seems to also be possible.",
